# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. Do not commit real secrets or production keys.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-visible (bundled into the browser — treat as public)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Browser → lead-studio-express-server (Express). Default in code is http://localhost:3032
# when unset in dev — set explicitly if your API port or host differs.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3032

# Optional: URL of this Next app (used for production URL detection and some helpers).
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only (Next.js route handlers / Node — never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# BFF / server-side proxy base when Next and Express run on different hosts.
EXPRESS_SERVER_URL=

# If you add protected Next `app/api` routes (e.g. cron or internal proxies), set this
# to match mentorai-server or your gateway secret — use only in server code, not in `src/api`.
CRON_SECRET=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local security hygiene (no extra env vars required)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# - If Express has no auth yet, bind it to 127.0.0.1 or firewall the port; do not expose
#   an open CRUD API on 0.0.0.0 without authentication.
# - Never put private keys in NEXT_PUBLIC_*; use server-only variables in route.ts instead.
